# PACE Retro — design.md

> Cutting-edge AI underneath, a 90s cartridge on top. PACE looks like the game you
> played after school and works like the sharpest tool on the desk: square paper
> cards with hard purple shadows, a pixel sky that follows the clock, and every
> name, rate and decision in plain, fast type. The personality lives in the frame
> (logo, sky, titles, icons); the work itself is calm.

## Instructions
- Pixel type is for the **frame only**: logo, page title, record title, log title (Press Start 2P); tabs and sidebar section labels (Silkscreen). Never on names, jobs, rates, buttons or body text.
- Everything has **square corners, an ink border and a hard, blur-free shadow**. No rounded corners, no soft shadows, no glass.
- Cards are **cream paper by day and dusk plum (`#221748`) at night** with cream text. (Cream cards at night were the first idea; the app gives cards and canvas one text colour, so a cream card would need dark text on a dark page — found building step 1.)
- **Sun Yellow is the single primary action** per screen (New Job, New Lead, Save). Decisions use the three muted state colours, never Sun Yellow.
- Colour on a list is scarce: one stage tag, one time tag, the trail. A record that is late gets a brick shadow and a brick id tab — not a red card.
- Numbers, rates, IDs and times are Space Mono so they line up; names are Hanken Grotesk 800.
- The mode follows the person's clock (light dawn–afternoon, dark dusk–night) unless they chose Light or Dark — saved **per person**, not per browser (D-0022).

## Brand & accent
- **Pixel Purple** `#7A4DE0` is the brand: active tab, AI match bar and score, record numbers.
- **Sun Yellow** `#FFD36E` is the one call to action and the selection outline.
- **Section colours** tell the two businesses apart at a glance: **My Day = Sage**, **Sales (lead generation) = Ochre**, **Recruiting = Lavender**. An active nav item takes its section's colour.

## Surface
- Light: canvas Arcade Cream `#F2EADB` with a faint 16px grid; sidebar Shelf Tan `#E8DCC6`.
- Dark: canvas Night `#130B2B` with the same grid in lavender at 5%; sidebar `#1D1240`.
- Cards and records: Cartridge Cream `#FFF6E6` by day, dusk plum `#221748` at night; 2px ink border app-wide (3px on the hero record and list cards). Controls: 2px border.
- The activity log is a green-screen monitor in both modes (CRT Black, phosphor text, scanlines).

## Text
- On cards: Midnight Ink `#1A1033` primary, Faded Ink `#6E6290` secondary.
- Straight on the canvas: `#5A4E7A` by day, Lavender Glow `#CDB8FF` at night.
- Page title on the sky: cream with a 3px black shadow, and **only over the upper (darker) bands** — every one of those is at least 3:1 against cream (day top band 4.8:1; the pale horizon bands are 1.2–2.5:1, so they carry only the sun, the moon and clouds). Small text on the sky (the date line) must sit over a band of 4.5:1 or better; on a phone, where the header stacks lower, it moves onto a cream chip.
- Measured (WCAG): faded ink on cream 5.1:1, ink on every state colour 6.8–10:1, cream on the purple tab 4.9:1, phosphor on CRT 15:1.

## Status & semantic
- Go / done = Sage. Stop / past due / not a fit = Brick (never fire-red). Waiting on you / needs detail = Ochre. Informational = Powder.
- As text on cream (YES, PASS, GAP): Leaf `#2E7D32` and Rust `#A0540C`.
- Stage words come from PACE's one stage vocabulary (`33-stage-modal.js`); the design never invents stage names.

## Fonts
- Press Start 2P and Silkscreen (pixel), Hanken Grotesk (body), Space Mono (data). All four are free (Google Fonts, OFL) and are **self-hosted** in `public/fonts/` — no third-party font request at runtime.

## Layout
- Desktop: sidebar 236px | list 430px | record (flexible) | decision column 196px; the activity log sits under the record.
- **The same three-pane pattern serves both businesses:**
  - Today / submissions: candidate list | submission | Send to client · Not a fit · Needs detail.
  - **Leads:** company list | lead (contacts, email history, AI brief) | Write email · Find contact · Release to pool.
  - Jobs: job list | job | Add candidate · Share apply link · Close.
- Sidebar sections: **MY DAY** (Today, My Team, Inbox, Reminders, Email) · **SALES** (Leads, Sourced Leads, Assign Leads, Clients, Lead Insights) · **RECRUITING** (Jobs / My Jobs + All Jobs, Candidates). A person sees only the sections their role uses; the role rules are unchanged from `renderSidebar`.

## Responsiveness
- Phone (≤600px): bottom bar of five, header stacks, nothing scrolls sideways, inputs 16px. An opened record shows a fixed three-button decision bar above the bottom bar, in thumb reach.
- Tablet: icon rail + record as a drawer.
- Hover effects only where a mouse exists (`hover:hover and pointer:fine`), never by width.

## Shape & geometry
- Radius 0. Borders 2px (controls) / 3px (surfaces). Dashed = not yet happened.
- Pixel art (sun, moon, clouds, icons, the duck) is drawn on a grid and rendered with crisp edges — never blurred, never scaled to a fractional pixel.

## Do
- Keep pixel type in the frame; keep data in Hanken / Space Mono.
- Use hard tinted shadows (plum by day, violet by night).
- Use one Sun Yellow action per screen.
- Give every nav item its own pixel icon.
- Let the sky carry the time of day; let the cards stay calm.
- Draw the AI match bar as one element (a mask), not one box per block.

## Don't
- Don't put the pixel font on buttons, names, tables or anything read under pressure.
- Don't use fire-red, lime or hot pink — the state colours are muted on purpose.
- Don't round corners, blur shadows or use glass.
- Don't animate anything on a timer that repaints the page; don't flip light/dark while someone is looking.
- Don't bring back the Duck Hunt scoreboard (D-0072); the duck appears only as a placement celebration.
- Don't use `transition: all`, inline colours or inline font sizes (R-013 classes only).
- Don't advertise what PACE does not do (no "verified", no fake system status).

## Signature
- **The clock sky:** banded dawn / day / dusk / night in the header and logo tile, with a pixel sun or crescent moon travelling an arc below the text.
- **The id tab:** every list card wears its record id in a small box hanging off its top-left edge (amber when selected, brick when late).
- **Hard purple shadows** under cream paper.
- **The green-screen activity log** — every change, who, when.
- **The PACE logo:** chunky pixel letters, lavender face, purple 3D extrusion, black outline.

## Notes
- **Decided:** retro direction (R-122); muted state colours; scoreboard out; the whole app follows day/night (D-0072); sidebar grouped by business (drawn 2026-10-06).
- **Open:** is this the look for every customer, or a theme they switch on? (Recommended: default for everyone, with Auto / Light / Dark saved per person.)
- **How it is built:** like the Session 23 re-skin (`docs/UI_REVAMP.md`, D-0015) — the tokens in `public/theme.css`, applied before first paint, the toggle touching one attribute. D-0015's three states become **Auto (clock) / Light / Dark**; "Auto" replaces "follow the operating system". Then the frame (sidebar, sky header), then the UI kit (`00-ui-kit.js` + `ui.css`), then screen by screen with a phone pass each.
- **Guards that must stay green:** `theme-contrast-smoke`, `mobile-layout-smoke`, `page-renders-smoke`, `utility-classes-smoke`, `nav-icons`, `screen-stability`.
- The reference mockups (concepts 1-3, sidebars by role) were built outside the app; they are pictures, not code to copy.
